@9020 = ~Torm's Hand
Randalla Brasshorn asked us to investigate a series of disappearances in Torm's Hand, a village north of Baldur's Gate. Her associates were sent there first but have not returned. We agreed to investigate the village and report back to Randalla.~
@9021 = ~Torm's Hand
We investigated the disappearances in Torm's Hand, uncovered what had happened to Randalla's missing associates, and returned to Randalla. She gave us the Bow of Silent Leaves as our reward. The matter is complete.~

// Randalla, Jaheira and Khalid English dialogue extracted for localisation.
@9022 = ~How did the investigation go?~
@9023 = ~We fulfilled the task and solved the mystery in Torm's Hand.~
@9024 = ~News of your success reached my ears through a messenger. He handed my Isaac's letter. He told me everything. An evil necromancer connected to Nine Hells posing as a Torm priestess? Unbelievable! But you did your part well, and as such here is your reward. That's little, but I've been told you've gained plenty from Nyriel himself. The Bow of Silent Leaves is yours.~
@9025 = ~News of your success reached my ears through a messenger. He handed my Isaac's letter. He told me everything. An evil necromancer connected to Nine Hells posing as a Torm priestess? Unbelievable! But you did your part well, and as such here is your reward. That's little, but I've been told you've gained plenty from Nyriel himself. The Bow of Silent Leaves is yours.~
@9026 = ~The Bow of Silent Leaves is yours. Its enchantments should serve you well.~
@9027 = ~Good to see you again.~
@9028 = ~Can I help you with something? How goes your investigation?~
@9029 = ~How do you know Jaheira exactly?~
@9030 = ~Still ongoing.~
@9031 = ~We worked under authority of Dermin Courtierdale - Jaheira's mentor. I was already a high agent for a long time, while Jaheira merely an adept. We quickly found common grounds however.~
@9032 = ~I was commanded by Jherek. I am his subordinate… although equal, I like to think. Jaheira and I were sent by our masters to retrieve an artifact called…~
@9033 = ~Very good. You aren't the same headstrong young adept that I had to babysit during that mission. Back then, you would've say what's on your mind without thinking beforehand. Glad to see you evolve into a fierce and independent fighter.~
@9034 = ~Still as pugnacious as ever. Some things never change. Anyway, we secured the artifact and held our own viciously against a small army of goblins. For a split second, we thought we were dead. They had us surrounded. Then, a loud bang echoed through the cave. Something caught goblins attention and we used this opportunity to flee. We ran out and noticed that reinforcements finally made it to help us.~
@9035 = ~Oh, Jaheira. Such eye for details. With your sharp perception and cocky attitude I unquestionably see you going up in the world. You show the backbone. I always respected that aspect of your personality.~
@9036 = ~It was nice catching up, Jaheira. I hope we satisfied your curiosity, <CHARNAME>.~
@9037 = ~Don't let me down.~
@9038 = ~Jaheira? Jaheira Elerrathin?~
@9039 = ~Welcome, adventurer. New in Baldur's Gate? My name is Randalla Brasshorn - merchant of local renown. You?~
@9040 = ~My name is <CHARNAME>. Pleased to make your acquaintance.~
@9041 = ~It was nice to meet you but we need to get going.~
@9042 = ~Momentarily unstable. We suffered some… setbacks as of late. We are picking ourselves up and dealing with it, however, we are persistent. And what companionship you took into your care. Gorion's Ward. Hero of Nashkel and active pawn in the game.~
@9043 = ~Since there is no need for secrecy and I see you are already aware of Jaheira's loyalties to Harpers organisation, I will not hold anything back from you, <CHARNAME>. Since you are here, I might need your help. Interested?~
@9044 = ~I might be interested. Firstly, we should speak about reward.~
@9045 = ~Sure. Tell me what needs to be done.~
@9046 = ~I am not interested. Find someone else.~
@9047 = ~Khalid Montenera, I'd wager. Jaheira told me about you last time we worked together. Impressive. You truly do seem as capable and valiant as Jaheira described. It's a pleasure to finally meet you.~
@9048 = ~Since there is no need for secrecy and I see you are already aware of Jaheira's loyalties to Harpers organisation, I will not hold anything back from you, <CHARNAME>. Since you are here, I might need your help. Interested?~
@9049 = ~I might be interested. Firstly, we should speak about reward.~
@9050 = ~Sure. Tell me what needs to be done.~
@9051 = ~I am not interested. Find someone else.~
@9052 = ~The <CHARNAME>? The saviour of Nashkel mines, and the whole region along with it? I would bow had I known your identity upon your arrival.~
@9053 = ~There is no need. I did what had to be done.~
@9054 = ~You should bow to your superior. That much is correct.~
@9055 = ~No need to be humble. I heard of your exploits and I must admit, I'm filled with admiration. You're an epitome of heroism and undoubtedly bards and singers already are generating tales and songs about your endeavours.~
@9056 = ~Hah. I like your attitude. Heed my advice though and be wary of that sort of privileged behaviour. As fun as you seem to be around, humility intact is an underestimated trait. Arrogance on the other hand is… irresponsible.~
@9057 = ~My contacts have watched you closely. I was briefed in on your progress. Honestly, I was taken by surprise that we met despite Baldur's Gate being such a massive place. Since you are here, I would like to present you the benefits of working for me. Interested?~
@9058 = ~Hold on. How do you know me so well? Who is your contact? Why are you following me?~
@9059 = ~I might be interested. Firstly, we should speak about reward.~
@9060 = ~Sure. Tell me what needs to be done.~
@9061 = ~I am not interested. Find someone else.~
@9062 = ~Alas, I am unauthorized to share that knowledge with you. What I can tell you is that my loyalties are with people who wish you all the success and foresee a great future for you. Our hopes are that you'll save the city from the darkness that dwells upon it.~
@9063 = ~Rest assured, you will get rewarded. As a wealthy merchant, I do come from money. I can also give you an object imbued with magical powers. Bow of Silent Leaves. Would you like to accept my offer?~
@9064 = ~Yes. I accept your offer.~
@9065 = ~Let's discuss the mission instead.~
@9066 = ~Fabolous. Mission I am about to sent you on needs to be taken care of subtly, as per my orders. Me and my cohorts were instructed to investigate a series of disappearances at Torm's Hand - a rural village just outside Baldur's Gate, to the north.~
@9067 = ~I understand. Each of us have our own roles to play. Our own assignments. In case you change your mind, you can find me here most of the time.~
@9068 = ~Interested?~
@9069 = ~I might be interested. Firstly, we should speak about reward.~
@9070 = ~Sure. Tell me what needs to be done.~
@9071 = ~I am not interested. Find someone else.~
@9072 = ~Our associates arrived at Torm's Hand few days ago and begun the search but we haven't heard from them. I cannot leave the city due to my own constrains, nor can I sent more co-workers whose hands are already full with other matters. Therefore, I need you.~
@9073 = ~Some time ago, before city gates were reopened, folk from the village begged Wyrm Crossing's guard to sent some soldiers down to the village. They declined due to restrictions that plaqued the city at a time, understandably so. We were able to sent our agents down there to investigate, however like I said before, to no avail. They didn't contact us back. I worry something went awry and things need checking out.~
@9074 = ~Torm's Hand is located just beyond the walls, simply follow the river until you reach it. Ask around, see what had happened and report back to me. You already proven yourself to be a menace, in the best way possible, so your support is my best bet. You've got your objective now. Please, don't tarry too long. Lives are at stake.~
@9075 = ~Randalla Brasshorn. It has been a long time since wind whispered your name to me. How are matters in the city?~
@9076 = ~<CHARNAME>. This is Randalla Brasshorn. Fellow harper, higher-ranking than me. We served together under Dermin Courtierdale's authority when our missions were intertwined a few years ago. Our cooperation proved fruitful and our labours highly productive toward greater cause.~
@9077 = ~Ekhem… Randalla. I'm afraid time is of the essence for us. Pleasantries will have to wait for later… (she looks at Khalid) much later.~
@9078 = ~Circumstances made it necessary.~
@9079 = ~That information is classified. Despite me knowing and mentoring <CHARNAME>, some details must remain shrouded in mystery.~
@9080 = ~I never had to be babysat. Besides, I seem to remember who saved who back when one of us was cornered by orcs in that cave. I'd struggle to think who is more headstrong and impulsive. Wouldn't you agree, Randalla?~
@9081 = ~That mission was doomed to fail the moment we set foot in that cave. Oh, my wording requires clearance… the moment Randalla set her foot in the cave, instead of awaiting reinforcements.~
@9082 = ~As difficult as it is to spit it out, you are a worthy and devoted Harper, even if a little extravagant and overly jovial for my taste.~
@9083 = ~Heh. Ehm… yes, I-it is a pleasure indeed.~
